<description>
Repeat the input tile across the output band indicated by the input's single solid row or column.

Input structure
The input is an n x n tile with exactly one full row or full column made of
one repeated color.

Rule
Create an n-by-n block canvas of black n x n blocks. If the solid guide is
row r, copy the input tile into every block of block row r. If the guide is
column c, copy the input tile into every block of block column c.

Key insight
The solid row or column is a control line: its orientation and index select
the row-band or column-band of the enlarged tiled canvas that remains visible.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "entire n x n input tile plus its single solid full row or full column as a guide line",
  "dst": "n x n grid of original-size blocks",
  "transform": "initialize all blocks to black; copy the input tile into every block of the guide row if the guide is horizontal, or every block of the guide column if the guide is vertical",
  "grid_shape": "n^2 x n^2 for an n x n input"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  input:
    grid: n x n square, n=3 [observed], solver supports any n>=2
    colors: exactly 3 distinct non-zero colors, no black (0)
    guide_line: exactly one full row or full column filled with a single color (the guide color)
    guide_position: any index 0..n-1, either row or column
    guide_color: does not appear in any non-guide cell
    non_guide_area: remaining (n-1)*n cells use exactly the other 2 colors freely
    constraint: no other row or column is entirely one color (exactly 1 solid line total)
  output:
    grid: n^2 x n^2 (e.g. 9x9 for n=3)
    structure: |
      Divide output into n x n blocks of size n x n each.
      If guide is row r: block-row r gets the input tile repeated n times; rest is black.
      If guide is col c: block-col c gets the input tile repeated n times; rest is black.

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (input is simple enough to generate directly)
  steps:
    1. Pick n (use 3 to match eval; solver supports 2-5).
    2. Pick guide orientation (row or column) and index (0..n-1).
    3. Choose 3 distinct non-zero colors; assign one as guide color.
    4. Fill the guide line (entire row or column) with the guide color.
    5. Fill remaining cells randomly with the other 2 colors.
    6. Verify no additional row or column is entirely one color; if so, resample that row/col.
```
